  ("All the critical pairs from this set of 10 rules can be reduced to the identity." 0.2282 0.8730 0.6573 0.6707 0.6707 0.0134 0.0069 0.2465 0.0250)
  ("These 10 rules are suﬃcient to solve the word problem for a free group with no other" 0.1812 0.8729 0.6769 0.6903 0.6903 0.0134 0.0053 0.2938 0.0490)
  ("properties. The word problem is to ﬁnd a decision procedure to decide whether any" 0.1812 0.8730 0.6965 0.7100 0.7100 0.0134 0.0060 0.2555 0.0888)
  ("two terms are equal, according to the axioms of group theory. The above rewrite" 0.1812 0.8730 0.7162 0.7296 0.7296 0.0134 0.0073 0.2455 0.0298)
  ("system can serve as a decision procedure by checking if the two terms have the same" 0.1812 0.8730 0.7358 0.7492 0.7492 0.0134 0.0052 0.2926 0.0571)
  ("canonical form." 0.1812 0.3092 0.7554 0.7688 0.7688 0.0134 0.0064 0.3063 0.0776)
  ("The above example illustrates the execution of the Knuth-Bendix completion" 0.2282 0.8730 0.7750 0.7884 0.7884 0.0134 0.0062 0.2814 0.0329)
  ("procedure, which is described by the following pseudo-code." 0.1812 0.6809 0.7947 0.8081 0.8081 0.0134 0.0064 0.2475 0.0877)
  ("Procedure 7.2.15. The procedure KnuthBendix(E, ) takes a set E of equations" 0.1812 0.8729 0.8206 0.8402 0.8379 0.0134 0.0064 0.2768 0.0988)
  ("and a simpliﬁcation order , and generates a canonical rewrite system from E when" 0.1812 0.8729 0.8402 0.8598 0.8575 0.0134 0.0051 0.3255 0.0308)
  ("it succeeds. It calls four procedures:" 0.1812 0.4828 0.8637 0.8771 0.8771 0.0134 0.0064 0.2059 0.0128))
  (262
  ("255" 0.8442 0.8729 0.0728 0.0862 0.0862 0.0134 nil 0.0000 0.0287)
  ("• pickEquation(E) will pick an equation from E;" 0.2099 0.6202 0.1242 0.1377 0.1377 0.0134 0.0064 0.3103 0.0096)
  ("• N F (t, R) returns a normal form of term t by R." 0.2099 0.6321 0.1564 0.1699 0.1699 0.0134 0.0064 0.3852 0.0096)
  ("• rewritable(t, r) will check if rewrite rule r can rewrite term t;" 0.2099 0.7375 0.1887 0.2021 0.2021 0.0134 0.0064 0.2955 0.0096)
