  ("and h(y, g(y)) = c. In general, if we have an equation s(x, z) = t(y, z), where x" 0.1812 0.8729 0.6853 0.6987 0.6987 0.0134 0.0079 0.2730 0.0308)
  ("does not appear in t and y does not appear in s, we may introduce a new function" 0.1812 0.8729 0.7049 0.7183 0.7183 0.0134 0.0064 0.2457 0.0368)
  ("h(z) to create two new equations: s(x, z) = h(z) and t(y, z) = h(z). For the" 0.1812 0.8729 0.7245 0.7379 0.7379 0.0134 0.0093 0.2659 0.0356)
  ("axioms AC = {(x ∗ y) ∗ y = x ∗ (y ∗ z), x ∗ y = y ∗ x}, we may consider the" 0.1812 0.8729 0.7403 0.7599 0.7576 0.0134 0.0070 0.2835 0.0580)
  ("rewriting over T (F, X)/=_{AC} , the so-called rewriting modulo AC (associativity and" 0.1812 0.8729 0.7638 0.7785 0.7772 0.0134 0.0063 0.3414 0.0754)
  ("commutativity)." 0.1812 0.3161 0.7834 0.7968 0.7968 0.0134 nil 0.3330 0.1350)
  ("When KnuthBendix terminates successfully, we obtain a canonical rewrite sys-" 0.2282 0.8729 0.8030 0.8164 0.8164 0.0134 0.0051 0.3262 0.0494)
  ("tem." 0.1812 0.2184 0.8227 0.8361 0.8361 0.0134 nil 0.3559 0.0372)
