  ("a simpliﬁcation order. Secondly, all the critical pairs of R are computed and each" 0.1812 0.8730 0.1439 0.1573 0.1573 0.0134 0.0070 0.2662 0.0096)
  ("pair is rewritten to the same term by R (if not, a new rule will be added into R)." 0.1812 0.8628 0.1635 0.1769 0.1769 0.0134 0.0064 0.3091 0.0329)
  ("To show that R is conﬂuent, we do induction on t based on . As a base case," 0.2282 0.8729 0.1793 0.1989 0.1965 0.0134 0.0055 0.2951 0.0218)
  ("if t is not rewritable by R, then R is conﬂuent trivially at t. Suppose, for i = 1, 2," 0.1812 0.8729 0.2028 0.2162 0.2162 0.0134 0.0067 0.2889 0.0112)
  ("t ⇒ t_{i} by l_{i} → r_{i} ∈ R at position p_{i} of t, i.e., t_{i} = t[p ↼ r_{i} σ_{i} ]." 0.1812 0.6900 0.2185 0.2381 0.2358 0.0134 0.0062 0.4810 0.0069)
